# 💬 What is a Large Language Model (LLM)?

A **Large Language Model (LLM)** is an AI model trained on large amounts of text and other data to understand and generate language.

LLMs can perform tasks such as:

* Answering questions
* Writing text
* Summarizing information
* Explaining concepts
* Translating languages
* Generating code
* Classifying text

```text
User Prompt
     │
     ▼
    LLM
     │
     ▼
Generated Response
```

---

# 🔤 What is a Token?

AI language models process text in smaller units called **tokens**.

A token may represent:

* A complete word
* Part of a word
* Punctuation
* Other text elements

Conceptually:

```text
Input Text
    │
    ▼
Tokens
    │
    ▼
Language Model
    │
    ▼
Output Tokens
    │
    ▼
Generated Text
```

> 💡 Tokens are the basic units used by language models when processing and generating text.

